{"TOCTOU race condition between CountDevices and CreateOrUpdateDevice allows concurrent requests to exceed deviceLimit under high concurrency": 0.7315656542778015, "ErrDeviceLimitReached is returned when rowsAffected == 0, but this also occurs when a known device's updated_at falls outside the 30-day BETWEEN window, incorrectly blocking legitimate returning users who were inactive for more than 30 days": 0.8141128420829773, "AnonymousDeviceLimit is declared as int64 (not *int64), so it serializes to 0 instead of null when no limit is configured, creating a type mismatch with the TypeScript type (number | undefined)": 0.568446695804596, "Duplicate thirtyDays constant in impl.go is not cleaned up alongside the new anonymousDeviceExpiration constant introduced in database.go and api.go": 0.23112764954566956}